{"task_id": "Mbpp/80", "solution": "def tetrahedral_number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth tetrahedral number.\n\n    A tetrahedral number is a figurate number that represents a pyramid\n    with a triangular base and three sides, called a tetrahedron.\n    The nth tetrahedral number is the sum of the first n triangular numbers.\n    Formula: T_n = n * (n + 1) * (n + 2) / 6\n\n    Args:\n        n: A positive integer representing the index of the tetrahedral number.\n\n    Returns:\n        The nth tetrahedral number.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If n is not a positive integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or n < 1:\n        raise ValueError(\n            f\"Input 'n' must be a positive integer (>= 1). Received: {n}\"\n        )\n    return (n * (n + 1) * (n + 2)) // 6"}
