{"task_id": "Mbpp/84", "solution": "from typing import Dict\nclass InvalidInputError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid input to Newman-Conway sequence calculation.\"\"\"\n    pass\ndef sequence(n: int, _memo: Dict[int, int] = None) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth Newman-Conway number using memoized recursion.\n    Raises InvalidInputError if n is not a positive integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if _memo is None:\n        _memo = {1: 1, 2: 1}\n\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or n < 1:\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"n must be a positive integer.\")\n\n    if n in _memo:\n        return _memo[n]\n\n    # C(n) = C(C(n - 1)) + C(n - C(n - 1))\n    val_n_minus_1 = sequence(n - 1, _memo)\n    val_c_n_minus_1 = sequence(val_n_minus_1, _memo)\n    val_n_minus_c_n_minus_1 = sequence(n - val_n_minus_1, _memo)\n\n    result = val_c_n_minus_1 + val_n_minus_c_n_minus_1\n    _memo[n] = result\n    return result"}
