{"task_id": "Mbpp/92", "solution": "def is_undulating(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if the input number is an undulating number.\n    Raises ValueError if input is not a positive integer.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(number, int) or number <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input must be a positive integer.\")\n\n    s_number = str(number)\n    n = len(s_number)\n\n    # Numbers with fewer than 3 digits are not considered undulating.\n    if n < 3:\n        return False\n\n    # Find the first two distinct digits.\n    digit1 = s_number[0]\n    digit2 = ''\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        if s_number[i] != digit1:\n            digit2 = s_number[i]\n            break\n    \n    # If no second distinct digit is found (e.g., 1111), it's not undulating.\n    if not digit2:\n        return False\n\n    # Check for the strictly alternating pattern.\n    for i in range(n):\n        if i % 2 == 0: # Digits at even indices should match digit1.\n            if s_number[i] != digit1:\n                return False\n        else: # Digits at odd indices should match digit2.\n            if s_number[i] != digit2:\n                return False\n    return True"}
