{"task_id": "Mbpp/92", "solution": "def is_undulating(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if an integer is an undulating number, meaning its digits strictly alternate (e.g., 12121).\n    Single-digit numbers are undulating, and negative numbers are checked by their absolute value.\n    \"\"\"\n    s = str(abs(number))\n    n = len(s)\n\n    if n <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    for i in range(n - 1):\n        if s[i] == s[i+1]:  # Digits must not be equal to the next digit\n            return False\n        if i + 2 < n and s[i] != s[i+2]:  # If s[i+2] exists, it must equal s[i]\n            return False\n    return True"}
