{"task_id": "Mbpp/80", "solution": "def tetrahedral_number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth tetrahedral number using the formula n * (n + 1) * (n + 2) / 6.\n\n    Args:\n        n: The non-negative integer for which to calculate the tetrahedral number.\n\n    Returns:\n        The nth tetrahedral number.\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: If n is not an integer.\n        ValueError: If n is a negative integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'n' must be an integer.\")\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a non-negative integer.\")\n    return n * (n + 1) * (n + 2) // 6"}
