{"task_id": "Mbpp/123", "solution": "def amicable_numbers_sum(limit: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of all amicable numbers up to a specified limit.\n    This function internally uses a helper to find sums of proper divisors.\"\"\"\n\n    if not isinstance(limit, int) or limit <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'limit' must be a positive integer.\")\n\n    def _sum_proper_divisors(n: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the sum of all proper divisors for a given positive integer.\n        Proper divisors exclude the number itself.\"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(n, int) or n <= 0:\n            # This check is defensive; 'amicable_numbers_sum' should pass valid positive integers.\n            raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a positive integer.\")\n        if n == 1:\n            return 0\n\n        total_sum = 1\n        # Efficiently find divisors up to the square root of n.\n        for i in range(2, int(n**0.5) + 1):\n            if n % i == 0:\n                total_sum += i\n                if i * i != n:\n                    total_sum += n // i\n        return total_sum\n\n    amicable_numbers_found = set()\n    total_amicable_sum = 0\n\n    # Iterate through numbers 'a' from 1 up to (but not including) the limit.\n    for a in range(1, limit):\n        if a in amicable_numbers_found:\n            continue\n\n        d_a = _sum_proper_divisors(a)\n\n        # Check conditions for a potential amicable pair (a, d_a).\n        if d_a > a and d_a < limit:\n            d_b = _sum_proper_divisors(d_a)\n\n            # If d_b equals 'a' and 'a' is distinct from 'd_a', it's an amicable pair.\n            if d_b == a and a != d_a:\n                total_amicable_sum += a + d_a\n                amicable_numbers_found.add(a)\n                amicable_numbers_found.add(d_a)\n\n    return total_amicable_sum"}
