{"task_id": "Mbpp/124", "solution": "import math\ndef angle_complex(real, imag):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the argument (angle) of a complex number (real + imag * j).\n    Returns the angle in radians, in the range (-pi, pi].\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(real, (int, float)):\n        raise TypeError(\"The 'real' part must be a numeric type (int or float).\")\n    _real_part = float(real)\n\n    if isinstance(imag, (int, float)):\n        _imag_part = float(imag)\n    elif isinstance(imag, complex):\n        _imag_part = imag.imag\n    else:\n        raise TypeError(\"The 'imag' part must be a numeric type (int, float, or complex).\")\n\n    return math.atan2(_imag_part, _real_part)"}
