{"task_id": "Mbpp/126", "solution": "import math\ndef _get_divisors(n: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds all positive divisors of a given positive integer n.\n    Returns a sorted list of divisors.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 0:\n        return []\n    divs = set()\n    for i in range(1, int(math.sqrt(n)) + 1):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            divs.add(i)\n            divs.add(n // i)\n    return sorted(list(divs))\ndef sum(num1: int, num2: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of all common divisors for two positive integers.\n    Raises ValueError for non-positive or non-integer inputs.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(num1, int) or not isinstance(num2, int):\n        raise ValueError(\"Inputs must be integers.\")\n    if num1 <= 0 or num2 <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Inputs must be positive integers.\")\n\n    common_divisor_candidate = math.gcd(num1, num2)\n    divisors = _get_divisors(common_divisor_candidate)\n    return __builtins__.sum(divisors)"}
