{"task_id": "Mbpp/222", "solution": "def check_type(data_tuple: tuple) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if all elements in the given tuple share the same data type.\n    Raises TypeError if the input argument is not a tuple.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(data_tuple, tuple):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a tuple.\")\n\n    # Returns True for empty tuples (FR4) and single-element tuples (FR5).\n    if len(data_tuple) <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    # For tuples with two or more elements, compare types.\n    first_element_type = type(data_tuple[0])\n    for element in data_tuple:\n        if type(element) is not first_element_type:\n            return False\n    return True"}
