{"task_id": "Mbpp/239", "solution": "import functools\ndef get_total_number_of_sequences(m: int, n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the number of possible sequences of length n,\n    where each element is a positive integer, is greater than or equal\n    to twice the previous element, and less than or equal to m.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(m, int) or m <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"m must be a positive integer.\")\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or n <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"n must be a positive integer.\")\n\n    @functools.lru_cache(None)\n    def _count_sequences_recursive(current_val: int, length_left: int) -> int:\n        if length_left == 0:\n            return 1  # Base case: a valid sequence of the required length is formed.\n\n        count = 0\n        # The next element must be at least twice the current and at most m.\n        for next_val in range(2 * current_val, m + 1):\n            count += _count_sequences_recursive(next_val, length_left - 1)\n        return count\n\n    total_sequences = 0\n    # The first element can be any positive integer from 1 to m.\n    for first_val in range(1, m + 1):\n        total_sequences += _count_sequences_recursive(first_val, n - 1)\n\n    return total_sequences"}
