{"task_id": "Mbpp/270", "solution": "from typing import List, Union\ndef sum_even_and_even_index(numbers: List[Union[int, float]]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of even numbers at even 0-indexed positions in a list.\n    Raises TypeError for non-list input or ValueError for non-numeric elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(numbers, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n\n    total_sum = 0\n    for index, number in enumerate(numbers):\n        if not isinstance(number, (int, float)):\n            raise ValueError(f\"List element at index {index} is not a number: {number}\")\n\n        # Check if both the number's value and its index are even.\n        if number % 2 == 0 and index % 2 == 0:\n            total_sum += int(number)\n\n    return total_sum"}
