{"task_id": "Mbpp/276", "solution": "import math\nfrom typing import Any\ndef _validate_positive_float(value: Any, name: str) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Validates if a given value is a non-negative float.\n    Raises TypeError if not a number, ValueError if negative.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(value, (float, int)):\n        raise TypeError(f\"{name} must be a number (float or int). Got {type(value).__name__}.\")\n    if value < 0:\n        raise ValueError(f\"{name} cannot be negative. Got {value}.\")\n    return float(value)\ndef volume_cylinder(radius: float, height: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the volume of a cylinder given its radius and height.\n    Raises TypeError or ValueError for invalid inputs.\n    \"\"\"\n    validated_radius = _validate_positive_float(radius, \"radius\")\n    validated_height = _validate_positive_float(height, \"height\")\n\n    volume = math.pi * (validated_radius ** 2) * validated_height\n    return volume"}
