{"task_id": "Mbpp/282", "solution": "from typing import List, Union\nclass ListSubtractionError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for list subtraction errors.\"\"\"\n    pass\ndef sub_list(list1: List[Union[int, float]], list2: List[Union[int, float]]) -> List[Union[int, float]]:\n    \"\"\"Subtracts two lists element-wise. Raises ListSubtractionError for length mismatches or non-numeric elements.\"\"\"\n    if len(list1) != len(list2):\n        raise ListSubtractionError(\"Lists must have the same length for element-wise subtraction.\")\n\n    result = []\n    for i in range(len(list1)):\n        val1 = list1[i]\n        val2 = list2[i]\n\n        if not isinstance(val1, (int, float)) or not isinstance(val2, (int, float)):\n            raise ListSubtractionError(\"Both lists must contain only numbers (int or float).\")\n\n        result.append(val1 - val2)\n    return result"}
