{"task_id": "Mbpp/306", "solution": "def max_sum_increasing_subseq(arr: list[int], n: int, i: int, k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence from arr[0...k]\n    such that arr[k] is included, and preceding elements are from arr[0...i].\n    \"\"\"\n    if not arr or n <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Array cannot be empty or have non-positive length.\")\n    if not (0 <= i < n and 0 <= k < n):\n        raise ValueError(\"Indices i and k must be within array bounds.\")\n    if i >= k:\n        raise ValueError(\"Index k must be strictly greater than index i.\")\n\n    # dp[j] stores the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence ending at arr[j] within arr[0...i].\n    dp = [arr[idx] for idx in range(i + 1)]\n\n    # Populate the dp array for all subsequences ending within arr[0...i].\n    for current_idx in range(i + 1):\n        for prev_idx in range(current_idx):\n            if arr[current_idx] > arr[prev_idx]:\n                dp[current_idx] = max(dp[current_idx], dp[prev_idx] + arr[current_idx])\n\n    # Find the maximum sum from dp where the ending element arr[j] is less than arr[k].\n    max_sum_before_k = 0\n    for j in range(i + 1):\n        if arr[j] < arr[k]:\n            max_sum_before_k = max(max_sum_before_k, dp[j])\n            \n    # The final sum includes arr[k]. If no valid preceding elements are found, max_sum_before_k is 0.\n    return max_sum_before_k + arr[k]"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/308", "solution": "from typing import List\nimport heapq\ndef large_product(list1: List[int], list2: List[int], k: int) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the k largest products formed by selecting one factor from each list.\n    Returns the products in descending order, raising ValueError for invalid inputs.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Validate input types and values for lists and k.\n    if not isinstance(list1, list) or not isinstance(list2, list):\n        raise ValueError(\"Inputs list1 and list2 must be lists.\")\n    if not all(isinstance(x, int) for x in list1) or not all(isinstance(x, int) for x in list2):\n        raise ValueError(\"All elements in list1 and list2 must be integers.\")\n    if not isinstance(k, int) or k < 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input k must be a positive integer.\")\n\n    # Handle cases where one or both lists are empty.\n    if not list1 or not list2:\n        return []\n\n    min_heap = [] # Use a min-heap to efficiently track the k largest products.\n\n    # Calculate all possible products and maintain the k largest in the heap.\n    for num1 in list1:\n        for num2 in list2:\n            product = num1 * num2\n            if len(min_heap) < k:\n                heapq.heappush(min_heap, product)\n            elif product > min_heap[0]:\n                heapq.heapreplace(min_heap, product)\n\n    # Sort the collected products in descending order before returning.\n    result = sorted(min_heap, reverse=True)\n    return result"}
