{"task_id": "Mbpp/389", "solution": "def find_lucas(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the n'th Lucas number. Raises ValueError for negative input or TypeError for non-integer input.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'n' must be an integer.\")\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a non-negative integer.\")\n    if n == 0:\n        return 2\n    if n == 1:\n        return 1\n\n    a, b = 2, 1  # Corresponds to L(0) and L(1)\n    for _ in range(2, n + 1):\n        a, b = b, a + b\n    return b"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/312", "solution": "import math\ndef volume_cone(radius: float, height: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the volume of a cone based on its radius and height.\n    Raises ValueError if radius or height are not positive numbers.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(radius, (int, float)) or radius <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Radius must be a positive number.\")\n    if not isinstance(height, (int, float)) or height <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Height must be a positive number.\")\n\n    volume = (1/3) * math.pi * (radius ** 2) * height\n    return volume"}
