{"task_id": "Mbpp/392", "solution": "class MemoizationStore:\n    \"\"\"\n    A simple in-memory store for memoization.\n    It uses a dictionary to cache computed results.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self):\n        self._cache = {}\n\n    def get(self, key: int) -> int | None:\n        \"\"\"Retrieves a value from the cache for a given key.\"\"\"\n        return self._cache.get(key)\n\n    def set(self, key: int, value: int) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Stores a key-value pair in the cache.\"\"\"\n        self._cache[key] = value\n\n    def has(self, key: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if a key exists in the cache.\"\"\"\n        return key in self._cache\nclass MaxSumSolver:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum sum for a given integer n using a recursive equation\n    and memoization to optimize performance.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, memo_store: MemoizationStore):\n        self._memo = memo_store\n\n    def get_max_sum(self, n: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Calculates the maximum sum for n, leveraging memoization for efficiency.\n        Handles base cases and recursive calls using integer division.\n        \"\"\"\n        if n <= 0:\n            return 0\n        \n        if self._memo.has(n):\n            return self._memo.get(n)\n\n        # Recursively calculate the sum of subproblems using integer division.\n        sum_val = self.get_max_sum(n // 2) + \\\n                  self.get_max_sum(n // 3) + \\\n                  self.get_max_sum(n // 4) + \\\n                  self.get_max_sum(n // 5)\n        \n        result = max(sum_val, n)\n        self._memo.set(n, result)\n        return result\n_global_memo = MemoizationStore()\n_global_solver = MaxSumSolver(_global_memo)\ndef get_max_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum sum for a given non-negative integer 'n'\n    based on the recursive equation f(n) = max( (f(n/2) + f(n/3) + f(n/4) + f(n/5)), n).\n    \"\"\"\n    return _global_solver.get_max_sum(n)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/395", "solution": "from collections import Counter\nfrom typing import Optional\ndef first_non_repeating_character(input_string: str) -> Optional[str]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the first character in a string that does not repeat.\n    Returns None if no such character exists or the string is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_string:\n        return None\n\n    char_counts = Counter(input_string)\n\n    for char in input_string:\n        if char_counts[char] == 1:\n            return char\n    return None"}
