{"task_id": "Mbpp/398", "solution": "def sum_of_digits(numbers: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the total sum of digits for all numbers in the given list.\n    Handles type validation and sums absolute digits for negative numbers.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(numbers, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'numbers' must be a list.\")\n\n    total_grand_sum = 0\n    for number in numbers:\n        if not isinstance(number, int):\n            raise TypeError(f\"All elements in 'numbers' must be integers. Found: {type(number).__name__}\")\n        \n        # Calculate sum of digits for a single number using its absolute value.\n        current_number_digit_sum = sum(int(digit_char) for digit_char in str(abs(number)))\n        total_grand_sum += current_number_digit_sum\n        \n    return total_grand_sum"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/398", "solution": "from typing import List\ndef _calculate_single_digit_sum(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of digits for a single non-negative integer.\n    This is a private helper function for modularity.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(number, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be an integer.\")\n    if number < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input number must be non-negative.\")\n\n    digit_sum = 0\n    num_str = str(number)\n    for digit_char in num_str:\n        digit_sum += int(digit_char)\n    return digit_sum\ndef sum_of_digits(numbers: List[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the total sum of digits for each number in a given list.\n    It orchestrates the digit sum calculation for all numbers provided.\n\n    Args:\n        numbers: A list of non-negative integers.\n\n    Returns:\n        The total sum of digits of all numbers in the list.\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: If the input is not a list or contains non-integer elements.\n        ValueError: If any number in the list is negative.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(numbers, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n\n    total_sum = 0\n    for num in numbers:\n        total_sum += _calculate_single_digit_sum(num)\n    return total_sum"}
