{"task_id": "Mbpp/428", "solution": "def shell_sort(array: list) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Sorts a list of comparable elements in-place using the Shell Sort algorithm.\n    The algorithm utilizes Knuth's gap sequence for optimal performance.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(array)\n    if n <= 1:\n        return\n\n    # Calculate initial gap using Knuth's sequence (h = h * 3 + 1).\n    h = 1\n    while h < n // 3:\n        h = h * 3 + 1\n\n    # Perform h-sort for decreasing gap sizes.\n    while h >= 1:\n        for i in range(h, n):\n            temp = array[i]\n            j = i\n            # Shift elements to make space for temp in the h-sorted sub-array.\n            while j >= h and array[j - h] > temp:\n                array[j] = array[j - h]\n                j -= h\n            array[j] = temp\n        h //= 3"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/429", "solution": "def and_tuples(tuple1: tuple[int, ...], tuple2: tuple[int, ...]) -> tuple[int, ...]:\n    \"\"\"Performs an element-wise bitwise AND operation on two input tuples of integers.\n    Raises TypeError for invalid input types/elements or ValueError for mismatched lengths.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(tuple1, tuple) or not isinstance(tuple2, tuple):\n        raise TypeError(\"Both inputs must be tuples.\")\n    if len(tuple1) != len(tuple2):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input tuples must have the same length.\")\n\n    result = []\n    for i in range(len(tuple1)):\n        if not isinstance(tuple1[i], int) or not isinstance(tuple2[i], int):\n            raise TypeError(\"All elements in tuples must be integers.\")\n        result.append(tuple1[i] & tuple2[i])\n    return tuple(result)"}
