{"task_id": "Mbpp/457", "solution": "from typing import Any, List, Optional\ndef Find_Min(list_of_lists: List[List[Any]]) -> Optional[List[Any]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the sublist with the minimum length from a given list of lists.\n    Returns the first such sublist if multiple share the minimum length, or None if the input is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(list_of_lists, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'list_of_lists' must be a list.\")\n\n    if not list_of_lists:\n        return None\n\n    min_length = float('inf')\n    min_sublist: Optional[List[Any]] = None\n\n    for sublist in list_of_lists:\n        # len() will implicitly raise TypeError if 'sublist' is not iterable.\n        current_length = len(sublist)\n        if current_length < min_length:\n            min_length = current_length\n            min_sublist = sublist\n            \n    return min_sublist"}
