{"task_id": "Mbpp/585", "solution": "from typing import List, Dict, Any\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nclass InvalidItemError(ValueError):\n    pass\ndef expensive_items(items: List[Dict[str, Any]], n: int) -> List[Dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the n most expensive items from a list of item dictionaries.\n    Handles various input scenarios including validation and sorting.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(items, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'items' must be a list.\")\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'n' must be an integer.\")\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' cannot be negative.\")\n\n    # Helper function to validate and convert a raw item dictionary to an Item object.\n    # Throws InvalidItemError for malformed item data.\n    def _validate_and_convert_item(item_data: Dict[str, Any]) -> Item:\n        if not isinstance(item_data, dict):\n            raise InvalidItemError(\"Each item must be a dictionary.\")\n        if 'name' not in item_data or not isinstance(item_data['name'], str):\n            raise InvalidItemError(\"Item must have a 'name' (string).\")\n        if 'price' not in item_data:\n            raise InvalidItemError(\"Item must have a 'price' key.\")\n        if not isinstance(item_data['price'], (int, float)):\n            raise InvalidItemError(\"Item 'price' must be a numeric value.\")\n        \n        return Item(name=item_data['name'], price=float(item_data['price']))\n\n    validated_items: List[Item] = []\n    for item_data in items:\n        try:\n            validated_items.append(_validate_and_convert_item(item_data))\n        except InvalidItemError as e:\n            # Re-raise as ValueError, providing context about the invalid item.\n            raise ValueError(f\"Invalid item data: {e.message} in item {item_data}\") from e\n\n    # Sort items by price in descending order.\n    # The slice [:n] correctly handles cases where n is greater than the list length.\n    sorted_items = sorted(validated_items, key=lambda item: item.price, reverse=True)[:n]\n\n    # Convert Item objects back to dictionaries for the return value.\n    return [item.__dict__ for item in sorted_items]"}
