{"task_id": "Mbpp/626", "solution": "def triangle_area(radius: float) -> float | None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the area of the largest triangle that can be inscribed\n    in a semicircle with the given radius.\n\n    The largest triangle in a semicircle has its base as the diameter\n    (2 * radius) and its height as the radius.\n    Area = 0.5 * base * height = 0.5 * (2 * radius) * radius = radius * radius.\n\n    Args:\n        radius: The radius of the semicircle.\n\n    Returns:\n        The area as a float if radius is non-negative, otherwise None.\n    \"\"\"\n    if radius < 0:\n        return None\n    return radius * radius"}
