{"task_id": "Mbpp/637", "solution": "def noprofit_noloss(cost_price: float | int, selling_price: float | int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a transaction resulted in no profit and no loss by comparing cost and selling prices.\n    Raises ValueError if inputs are not numeric.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(cost_price, (int, float)) or not isinstance(selling_price, (int, float)):\n        raise ValueError(\"Both cost_price and selling_price must be numeric.\")\n    \n    return cost_price == selling_price"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/635", "solution": "def _heapify(data_list: list, n: int, i: int) -> None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Helper function to maintain the heap property in a subtree rooted at index i.\n    n is the size of the heap (number of elements to consider).\n    \"\"\"\n    largest = i\n    left = 2 * i + 1\n    right = 2 * i + 2\n\n    if left < n and data_list[largest] < data_list[left]:\n        largest = left\n\n    if right < n and data_list[largest] < data_list[right]:\n        largest = right\n\n    if largest != i:\n        data_list[i], data_list[largest] = data_list[largest], data_list[i]\n        _heapify(data_list, n, largest)\n\ndef heap_sort(data_list: list) -> None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a list in ascending order using the heap sort algorithm in-place.\n    Raises TypeError if data_list is not a list.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(data_list, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n\n    n = len(data_list)\n\n    # Build a maxheap, starting from the last parent node up to the root.\n    for i in range(n // 2 - 1, -1, -1):\n        _heapify(data_list, n, i)\n\n    # Extract elements one by one from the heap and place them at the end of the list.\n    for i in range(n - 1, 0, -1):\n        data_list[i], data_list[0] = data_list[0], data_list[i]\n        _heapify(data_list, i, 0)"}
