{"task_id": "Mbpp/806", "solution": "def max_run_uppercase(input_string: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the maximum length of a consecutive sequence of uppercase characters within the input string.\n    Raises TypeError for non-string input, and returns 0 for empty strings or those with no uppercase characters.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(input_string, str):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a string.\")\n\n    max_run = 0\n    current_run = 0\n\n    for char in input_string:\n        if char.isupper():\n            current_run += 1\n        else:\n            max_run = max(max_run, current_run)\n            current_run = 0\n    \n    # Final check in case the string ends with an uppercase run\n    max_run = max(max_run, current_run)\n    \n    return max_run"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/806", "solution": "def max_run_uppercase(text: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the maximum number of consecutive uppercase characters in the given string.\n    Raises TypeError if the input is not a string.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(text, str):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a string.\")\n\n    max_run = 0\n    current_run = 0\n    for char in text:\n        if char.isupper():\n            current_run += 1\n        else:\n            current_run = 0\n        max_run = max(max_run, current_run)\n    return max_run"}
